## Purpose of this document
 
This document records the complete design of the ViewCastLK forecasting model: the modelling
approach, the exact feature set, how each feature is produced, how the model is trained and
validated, what metrics are reported, what the dashboard sends to the model and receives back,
and who owns which piece of work.
 
It is written to be:
 
1. **Approved by the team** — every design decision is stated explicitly so that agreement or
   disagreement can be recorded before implementation begins.
2. **Executed by Claude Code** — Sections 4 through 10 are specific enough to be handed to an
   agent as an implementation specification.
3. **Reused in the final report** — the rationale for each decision is written out, not just the
   decision itself.
Items that are **not yet decided** are collected in Section 12 (Open Decisions) rather than being
silently assumed. Nothing in Section 12 blocks the start of implementation.
 
