## 2. Data Source and Starting Point
 
The model consumes the `ml_video_features` view already built on the Supabase PostgreSQL
warehouse. That view is one row per video and already contains:
 
- Publication metadata (timestamp, category, duration, definition, caption, made-for-kids flag,
  language fields)
- Pre-derived title features (length, word count, number/question/exclamation flags, uppercase
  ratio, script)
- Channel-state-at-publish snapshots (subscribers, views, video count, channel age)
- The four horizon targets with accompanying quality flags (`d*_hours_off`, `d*_usable`)
- Row-level gating flags (`eligible`, `is_live_broadcast`, `channel_stats_backfilled`)
As of the feasibility study the pipeline had collected 95,768 engagement snapshots across 6,870
videos from 377 channels covering 14 of the 15 target categories. The 40-day collection window
continues to accumulate data, so all volume figures in this plan are lower bounds.
 
**The model layer treats `ml_video_features` as its contract with the pipeline layer.** Any new
feature the model needs must be added to that view by the pipeline owner, not computed ad hoc in a
notebook.
 
