## 3. Row Selection: which videos enter training
 
Rows are filtered in this order, and the count dropped at each stage is logged (this table goes
into the final report):
 
| Step | Rule | Reason |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | `eligible = true` | Existing pipeline-level validity gate |
| 2 | `is_live_broadcast = false` | Live streams have a fundamentally different view accumulation pattern and would pollute the training signal |
| 3 | At least one horizon has `d*_usable = true` | A row with no usable target teaches the model nothing |
| 4 | `channel_stats_backfilled` recorded, not filtered | Backfilled channel stats are kept but flagged, so their effect can be tested during ablation |
 
**Videos with fewer than 30 days of tracking are kept.** They are not excluded. See Section 5.3.
 
**Outlier handling:** apply the 3-sigma filter described in the project proposal, but apply it on
the **log scale** of the target, not the raw scale. On the raw scale a genuinely viral Sri Lankan
video would be discarded as an outlier when it is in fact the most interesting row in the dataset.
On the log scale only corrupted or impossible records are removed. The number of rows removed and
a sample of them is documented.
 
